+    // caused a full swapchain teardown/rebuild on literally every frame, all
+    // session long, on affected devices (confirmed via a tester log: ~4800
+    // recreations in a single play session). That's a huge amount of pointless
+    // Vulkan resource churn stressing any latent resource-lifetime race far
+    // more than normal play would. Real resize/format/present-mode changes
+    // already flow through their own dedicated setSurfaceExtent() /
+    // setSurfaceFormat() / setSyncInterval() calls above, which set
+    // m_dirtySwapchain independently -- so it's safe to only force a recreate
+    // here on an actual failure (negative VkResult, e.g. VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DATE_KHR
+    // or VK_ERROR_SURFACE_LOST_KHR), not on the informational VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR.
+    if (status < 0) {
       Logger::info(str::format("Presenter: Got ", status, ", recreating swapchain"));
 
       m_dirtySwapchain = true;
